{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27272459","formula":"C₁₉H₁₇ClN₆O₂","hill":"C19H17ClN6O2","elements":["H","C","N","O","Cl"],"composition":{"C":19.0,"H":17.0,"N":6.0,"O":2.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"Ketodarolutamide"},"descriptions":{"en":"Ketodarolutamide (developmental code names ORM-15341, BAY-1896953) is a nonsteroidal antiandrogen (NSAA) and the major active metabolite of darolutamide (ODM-201, BAY-1841788), an NSAA which is used in the treatment of prostate cancer in men. Similarly to its parent compound, ketodarolutamide acts as a highly selective, high-affinity, competitive silent antagonist of the androgen receptor (AR). Both agents show much higher affinity and more potent inhibition of the AR relative to the other NSAAs enzalutamide and apalutamide, although they also possess much shorter and comparatively less favorable elimination half-lives."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":52919826,"mass":396.8,"charge":0,"smiles":"C[C@@H](CN1C=CC(=N1)C2=CC(=C(C=C2)C#N)Cl)NC(=O)C3=CC(=NN3)C(=O)C","inchikey":"GMBPVBVTPBWIKC-NSHDSACASA-N","iupac":"3-acetyl-N-[(2S)-1-[3-(3-chloro-4-cyanophenyl)pyrazol-1-yl]propan-2-yl]-1H-pyrazole-5-carboxamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"52919826","atoms":45,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.681,"y":-2.407,"z":-0.13,"el":"Cl"},{"x":3.851,"y":0.608,"z":1.693,"el":"O"},{"x":1.25,"y":-5.342,"z":-0.249,"el":"O"},{"x":0.778,"y":3.269,"z":-0.486,"el":"N"},{"x":2.834,"y":1.106,"z":-0.33,"el":"N"},{"x":0.004,"y":2.189,"z":-0.683,"el":"N"},{"x":3.028,"y":-2.127,"z":1.496,"el":"N"},{"x":2.537,"y":-3.332,"z":1.159,"el":"N"},{"x":-6.372,"y":-1.848,"z":0.225,"el":"N"},{"x":3.199,"y":2.504,"z":-0.362,"el":"C"},{"x":2.149,"y":3.334,"z":-1.117,"el":"C"},{"x":4.575,"y":2.665,"z":-1.0,"el":"C"},{"x":0.203,"y":4.223,"z":0.3,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.102